        "orario": "18:10",
        "timestamp": 1782058236,
        "contenuto_esteso": "To display this content from YouTube, you must enable advertisement tracking and audience measurement. One of your browser extensions seems to be blocking the video player from loading. To watch this content, you may need to disable it on this site. Trump threatens to strike Iran over support for Hezbollah as fighting continues in Lebanon Middle East Issued on: 21/06/2026 - 18:10 US President Donald Trump on Sunday threatened to strike Iran if it did not stop Hezbollah from \"causing trouble,\" as peace talks between senior US and Iranian officials began in Switzerland. The memorandum of understanding signed Wednesday between the United States and Iran stipulates a cessation of hostilities on all fronts, including in Lebanon. But Israeli strikes on Lebanon continued -- in response, they say, to projectiles fired by the Iran-backed group at its troops. Details and analysis by FRANCE 24 international affairs editor Kethevane Gorjestani. Israeli strikes start again in Lebanon after several-hour lull, amid US-Iran talks 21/06/2026 Middle East Sailors trapped in Hormuz strait, dodging drones and rationing food 21/06/2026 Middle East Israel and Hezbollah trade fire, as US-Iran talks begin in Switzerland 21/06/2026 Middle East Iran claims Lebanon 'main topic' at peace talks with US 21/06/2026 Middle East US-Iran peace talks to begin, after Tehran closed Strait of Hormuz 21/06/2026 Middle East Iran closes Strait of Hormuz despite ceasefire after continued Israeli strikes in Lebanon 20/06/2026 Middle East Israel strikes Lebanon despite ceasefire, at least 16 killed 20/06/2026 Middle East NGOs in Lebanon denounce Israeli attacks on medics amid ceasefire 20/06/2026 Middle East Could Israel lose Donald Trump’s support by continuing to drop bombs in Lebanon? 20/06/2026 Middle East"
